  rankdir="TB";
  "AI_Rule" [label="(0,0,0) If there is need for multidisciplinary LCS implementation and there exists vast multimodal data plus multiple clinical tasks, then AI promises to significantly improve LCS quality and efficiency."];
  "Challenge_Common" [label="(0,0,0) The common is that these operational and resource barriers collectively hinder real-world screening uptake and impact."];
  "DL_Common" [label="(0,0,0) The common is that task-specific models on small single-modality datasets with costly bounding-box annotations inherently limit multitask performance and scalability."];
  "Effect_Common" [label="(0,0,0) The common is that randomized controlled trials reliably demonstrate effective mortality reduction for screening interventions."];
  "Effect_Concl" [label="(0,0,0) induction-reasoning: Currently there is that LCS with LDCT reduces lung cancer mortality in major trials (NLST/NELSON), and the common is that randomized controlled trials reliably demonstrate effective mortality reduction for screening interventions, so LCS with LDCT is effective in reducing lung cancer mortality."];
  "FM_Common" [label="(0,0,0) The common is that large-scale pretraining on heterogeneous data enables adaptable, high-performance unified task handling across domains."];
  "FM_Concl" [label="(0,0,0) induction-reasoning: Currently there is that FMs demonstrate unseen abilities for diverse data and unified multitask execution, updating SoTA across NLP/CV/multimodal and inspiring medical FMs, and the common is that large-scale pretraining on heterogeneous data enables adaptable, high-performance unified task handling across domains, so foundation models provide a breakthrough paradigm for multimodal multitask learning."];
  "NROOT" [label="(0,0,0) This work aims to develop and evaluate a scalable lung-cancer-screening data-curation pipeline that aligns 3-D low-dose CT/CT scans with clinical information, and to build the Medical Multimodal Multitask Foundation Model M3FM—using imaging, text/clinical, task-conditioning and prediction components—to support many LCS tasks, address limitations of task-specific or single-modality AI models, and enable more efficient lung cancer screening workflows.", fillcolor="lightyellow", style="filled"];
  "NROOT_COMMON" [label="(0,0,0) When an effective screening program faces workflow barriers and existing AI/foundation-model methods cannot fully handle multimodal, multitask 3-D CT screening data, a scalable curation pipeline plus a multimodal multitask foundation model is a justified research direction."];
  "Need_Concl" [label="(0,0,0) deduction-reasoning: Currently there is that LCS is effective in reducing mortality but faces significant challenges, and if LCS is effective in reducing mortality but faces significant challenges, then there is an important and immediate need for multidisciplinary efforts to implement LCS broadly, equitably, and optimally, so there is an important and immediate need for multidisciplinary efforts to broadly, equitably, and optimally implement LCS."];
  "Proposal_Know" [label="(0,0,0) Knowledge: Integrated scalable data curation combined with foundation-model architecture can overcome dimensionality/curation barriers and enable unified multitask performance."];
  "R10" [label="(0,0,0) LCS faces operational and resource challenges including low uptake, false positives, suboptimal workflows, multimodal data under-utilization and radiologist shortage."];
  "R11" [label="(0,0,0) LCS is supported as mortality-reducing while also facing substantial real-world operational and resource barriers."];
  "R12" [label="(0,0,0) Because LCS can reduce mortality yet faces substantial barriers, there is motivation for multidisciplinary efforts to implement LCS broadly, equitably and optimally."];
  "R13" [label="(0,0,0) The combination of LCS implementation need, accumulated multimodal LCS data and multiple clinical tasks motivates using AI to improve LCS quality and efficiency."];
  "R14" [label="(0,0,0) Existing LCS AI models are limited by task-specific, small single-modality datasets and costly annotation requirements, which restrict scalability for multitask workflows."];
  "R15" [label="(0,0,0) Foundation models have demonstrated broad ability to handle diverse data types and unified multitask execution across NLP, computer vision, multimodal understanding and emerging medical settings."];
  "R16" [label="(0,0,0) Existing foundation models have not effectively handled varied LCS tasks with multimodal clinical data, particularly 3-D LDCT scans, because of data-curation and model-architecture barriers."];
  "R17" [label="(0,0,0) Foundation-model evidence supports the knowledge that large-scale models can provide adaptable, unified multitask handling for diverse data in general and medical domains."];
  "R18" [label="(0,0,0) The paper proposes integrated scalable data curation aligning high-dimensional images with clinical datasets for 17 LCS tasks and develops M3FM to process 3-D CT volumes plus clinical data for multiple LCS tasks."];
  "R5" [label="(0,0,0) Deep-learning approaches have produced promising LCS results, but current task-specific, small single-modality and annotation-intensive models motivate more scalable multitask approaches rather than fully solving LCS workflow needs."];
  "R9" [label="(0,0,0) Evidence from major LDCT screening trials supports that LCS with LDCT reduces lung-cancer mortality."];
  "S12" [label="(12,0,0) Currently there is that LCS-related AI models were developed with small single-modality datasets for individual tasks, limiting performance/utility in multitask workflow."];
  "S14" [label="(14,0,0) Currently there is that foundation models have shown previously unseen abilities to understand diverse data types and execute many tasks unified."];
  "S17" [label="(17,0,0) Currently there is that none of existing FMs can perform variety of LCS tasks interpreting multimodal clinical data, particularly 3D LDCT scans."];
  "S18" [label="(18,0,0) Currently there is that the limitation is primarily due to challenges in data curation and model architecture."];
  "S2" [label="(2,1,0) Currently there is that LCS with LDCT reduces lung cancer mortality by 20% in NLST."];
  "S23" [label="(23,0,0) Currently there is that we present an integrated scalable data curation approach to align high-dimensional images with clinical datasets for 17 LCS tasks and 49 elements."];
  "S3" [label="(3,0,0) Currently there is that LCS faces challenges (low rate <10%, high false-positive, sub-optimal workflows, multimodal under-utilization, radiologist shortage)."];
